{%- comment -%}
  Renders a locale-aware label for a Shopify product's `type` field.

  `product.type` is a free-text field the merchant enters once, in whatever
  language they were using at the time (this store's product types were
  entered in Spanish: "Comederos", "Descanso", "Paseo") — it does NOT change
  with the storefront locale like `| t` strings do. Printing `{{ type }}`
  directly (as this theme did before) means the English storefront still
  shows the Spanish category name.

  This snippet maps the known type values to a `collections.category.*`
  locale key (translated in both locales/es.default.json and locales/en.json)
  and falls back to the raw `type` string for anything not in the mapping —
  so a new/unmapped product type never breaks or shows "translation missing",
  it just behaves exactly like before this fix.

  Usage: {% render 'product-type-label', type: product.type %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- case type -%}
  {%- when 'Comederos' -%}{{ 'collections.category.feeding' | t }}
  {%- when 'Descanso' -%}{{ 'collections.category.rest' | t }}
  {%- when 'Paseo' -%}{{ 'collections.category.walking' | t }}
  {%- when 'Grooming' -%}{{ 'collections.category.grooming' | t }}
  {%- else -%}{{ type }}
{%- endcase -%}
